// Title: Code blocks in the automatically produced visualizer for Nile programs (right column)
// Author: not credited on the figure page
// Source: VPRI TR-2012-001 (STEPS 2012 final report), Section 3 "Inventing methods that create automatic visualizers
//         for languages created from metalanguages"; figure captioned "Automatically produced visualizer for the Nile
//         programs that convert a Bezier curve (at top left) to shaded pixels (bottom columns). The right column is an
//         expansion of the 'Texture' code block."; PDF page 13 (printed page 12). Five code blocks, top to bottom.
// Transcribed from the page images (raster figure, no text layer); text-layer differences noted below.
ExpandSpans () : SpanCoverage >> PointCoverage
    ∀ (x, y, c, l)
        if c > 0 ∧ l > 0
            >> (x, y, c)
            << (x + 1, y, c, l - 1)

ProjectLinearGradient (A:Point, B:Point) : PointCoverage >> Real
    v   = B - A
    Δs  = v / (v · v)
    s00 = A · Δs
    ∀ (P,_)
        >> P · Δs - s00

PadGradient () : Point >> Point
    ∀ s
        >> 0 ▷ s ◁ 1

GradientSpan (A:Color, B:Color) : Real >> Color
    ∀ s
        >> sA + (1 - s)B

ZipPixels () : (PointCoverage, Color) >> Pixel
    ∀ ((x, y, coverage), (r, g, b, a))
        >> ((x, y), (r, g, b, a * coverage))

// Transcription notes
// - [?] Glyph shapes at the figure's resolution: "∀" (for all), "∧" (and), "◁" and "▷" (triangle operators),
//   "·" (dot product), "Δ" (delta) and "≪"/"<<" were read from the image; the arrow operators in the
//   ExpandSpans and ProjectLinearGradient blocks are read as printed.
// - [?] In ProjectLinearGradient the second-to-last line reads "V (P,_)" in the image; the glyph is read as "∀"
//   by parallel with the other blocks (the same symbol appears as "V" at the figure's resolution).
// - Indentation reproduced from the image; exact space counts may differ.
// - The figure's right column is the expanded code the caption refers to; it is not the "Texture" block
//   itself, which lies in the left panel of the figure and is not transcribed here.
